..Fiscal Note
The proposed resolution authorizes a sole source service contract with Stryker Sales Corporation - Medical Division for annual preventative maintenance and service for ambulance power cot and power load systems. The annual cost of this three-year contract is $45,264.60 for a total cost over the three years of $135,793.80. This contract is included in the Fire Department’s adopted budget. No additional appropriation required.
..Title
A Resolution authorizing a sole source contract between Stryker Sales Corporation - Medical Division (Stryker) as the only contractor who can perform annual preventative maintenance and service for ambulance power cot and power load systems. (Citywide)
..Body
WHEREAS, the Fire Department has purchased and implemented Stryker Power Load Systems and Power Cots in all front line and reserve ambulance units;

WHEREAS, the Ambulance Power Cots and Power Load systems require annual maintenance and occasional repair to maintain optimum performance;

WHEREAS, Stryker utilizes proprietary diagnostic tools and software when servicing the Power Load systems and maintains its own field service team to perform maintenance using only parts manufactured specifically for Stryker products;

WHEREAS, Fire Department staff have negotiated a 3-year, no increase service contract with Stryker for a cost of $45,264.60 per year, totaling $135,793.80;

WHEREAS, the contract will include two 1-year options for renewal with no price increase;

WHEREAS, equipment support and maintenance contracts of $50,000 or more that are not competitively selected must meet one of the exceptions stated in MGO 4.26(4)(a) and require Common Council approval and Mayor and Clerk signature;

WHEREAS, this contract meets the exception in MGO 4.26(4)(a)2., “the service required is available from only one person or firm” because only Stryker can support and maintain its Power Load Cot systems, as explained in the attached Noncompetitive Selection Request Form;

NOW THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, the Mayor and City Clerk are authorized to sign a three-year contract with Stryker Sales Corporation - Medical Division for repair and maintenance of ambulance power cot and power load systems at a total price of $135,793.80, starting in 2024;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that should the Madison Fire Department choose up to two 1-year options for contract renewal with no price increase, the Madison Fire Chief is authorized to sign the renewals.

..Fiscal Note
The proposed resolution authorizes a noncompetitive, sole source purchase of 3M Scott cylinders for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) used by the Madison Fire Department. The total purchase amount is approximately $126,150. Funding is available in the Fire Department's 2025 Adopted Capital Budget (Munis #17225). No additional appropriation is required. 
..Title
Authorizing a non-competitive purchase of goods from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc., as a sole source provider of 3M Scott fire and safety products serving Dane County, WI that is trained and authorized to provide these products.
..Body
WHEREAS, the Madison Fire Department currently uses 3M Scott cylinders for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) and needs to replace aging cylinders;

WHEREAS, an alternative cylinder would require the purchase of different SCBAs;

WHEREAS, the estimated cost of the 3M Scott cylinders and its components is $126,150;

WHEREAS, it is both economical and operationally seamless to continue to use 3M Scott cylinders;

WHEREAS, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only provider of 3M Scott products in Dane County, Wisconsin for public fire protection agencies;

WHEREAS, for the reasons stated above and in the attached noncompetitive selection request form, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only vendor that can provide for the specific needs of the Madison Fire Department;

WHEREAS, MGO 4.26(2) requires goods to be purchased using a competitive process approved by the Finance Director, and under the Finance Director’s Purchasing Guidelines, Common Council approval is required to purchase goods of $50,000 or more without a competitive process;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, the Common Council authorizes the purchase of goods described above from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc.

..Fiscal Note
The proposed resolution authorizes a noncompetitive, sole source purchase of 3M Scott cylinders, harnesses, and facepieces for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) used by the Madison Fire Department. The total purchase amount is approximately $1,040,820. Funding is available in the Fire Department's 2025 Adopted Capital Budget (Munis #17225). No additional city appropriation is required.

..Title
Authorizing a noncompetitive purchase of goods from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc., as a sole source provider of 3M Scott fire and safety products serving Dane County, WI, for the replacement of all self-contained breathing apparatuses used by the City of Madison Fire Department.

..Body
WHEREAS, the Madison Fire Department (MFD) currently uses 3M Scott cylinders, harnesses, and facepieces for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) and needs to replace the aging components;

WHEREAS, 93 cylinders were decommissioned in January 2025 due to failed inspection (15+ years old) and an additional 285 cylinders will be decommissioned over the next three years; 

WHEREAS, an alternative cylinder would require the purchase of different SCBAs;

WHEREAS, the expenditure for the full replacement of all of MFD’s SCBA units was authorized in the 2024 adopted capital budget;

WHEREAS, the estimated cost of the 3M Scott cylinders and SCBA components is $1,040,820.00;

WHEREAS, it is both economical and operationally seamless to continue to use 3M Scott cylinders;

WHEREAS, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only provider of 3M Scott products in Dane County, Wisconsin for public fire protection agencies;

WHEREAS, for the reasons stated above and in the attached noncompetitive selection request form, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only vendor that can provide for the specific needs of the Madison Fire Department;

WHEREAS, MGO 4.26(2) requires goods to be purchased using a competitive process approved by the Finance Director, and under the Finance Director’s Purchasing Guidelines, Common Council approval is required to purchase goods of $75,000 or more without a competitive process;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, the Common Council authorizes the purchase of goods described above from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc.

..Fiscal Note
The proposed resolution authorizes a noncompetitive, sole source purchase of 3M Scott cylinders for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) used by the Madison Fire Department in the amount of $96,960. Funding is available in the Fire Department's 2026 Adopted Capital Budget (Munis #17225). No additional appropriation is required.

..Title
Authorizing a noncompetitive purchase of goods from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc., as a sole source provider of 3M Scott fire and safety products serving Dane County, WI, for cylinders for self-contained breathing apparatuses used by the City of Madison Fire Department.

..Body
WHEREAS, the Madison Fire Department (MFD) currently uses 3M Scott cylinders, harnesses, and facepieces for self-contained breathing apparatuses (SCBA) and needs to replace the aging components;

WHEREAS, 93 cylinders were decommissioned in January 2025 due to failed inspection (15+ years old) and an additional 285 cylinders will be decommissioned over the next three years;

WHEREAS, an alternative cylinder would require the purchase of different SCBAs;

WHEREAS, 3M Scott has announced a six percent (6%) fuel and energy cost increase effective May 1, 2026 in addition to their annual product pricing increase;

WHEREAS, it would be fiscally prudent to purchase cylinders prior to the price increase;

WHEREAS, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only provider of 3M Scott products in Dane County, Wisconsin for public fire protection agencies;

WHEREAS, for the reasons stated above and in the attached noncompetitive selection request form, Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc. is the only vendor that can provide for the specific needs of the Madison Fire Department;

WHEREAS, the estimated cost of the 3M Scott cylinders and SCBA components is $96,960;

WHEREAS, MGO 4.26(2) requires goods to be purchased using a competitive process approved by the Finance Director, and under the Finance Director’s Purchasing Guidelines, Common Council approval is required to purchase goods of $75,000 or more without a competitive process;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, the Common Council authorizes the purchase of cylinders from Jefferson Fire & Safety, Inc.
